  "$comment": "letibot: what never asks. opencode's shape: a tool, then a pattern over its path or, for bash, over ONE simple command as a prefix; allow | deny | ask; the last matching rule wins, so put a deny after the pattern it narrows. A compound command is tested one simple command at a time; a substitution, a redirection to a file, a group, a here-doc or a leading VAR= is never matched. `Always allow` on a prompt appends here. This file was installed once from the repository's config/permission.json and is yours from then on. Groups: git, read-only; gh, read-only; rust; go; other test runners; the shell's read-only utilities",
